[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Not Very Musical]
[00:00.66]What happened when the snake charmer began to play jazz? | 耍蛇人开始演奏爵士乐时发生了什么？
[00:15.22]As we had had a long walk through one of the markets of old Delhi, | 我们在老德里的一处市场走了很长一段路之后，
[00:21.68]we stopped at a square to have a rest. | 在一个广场停下来休息。
[00:25.48]After a time, we noticed a snake charmer with | 过了一会儿，我们注意到广场的另一边有位耍蛇人，
[00:29.74]two large baskets at the other side of the square, | 带着两个大篮子。
[00:33.76]so we went to have a look at him. | 于是我们走过去看他。
[00:37.02]As soon as he saw us, | 他一看到我们，
[00:39.68]he picked up a long pipe which was covered with coins and opened one of the baskets. | 便拿起一根盖满硬币的长笛，打开了一个篮子。
[00:46.59]When he began to play a tune, | 当他开始吹奏曲子时，
[00:49.68]we had our first glimpse of the snake. | 我们第一次瞥见了那条蛇。
[00:53.48]It rose out of the basket and began to follow the movements of the pipe. | 它从篮子里钻出来，开始跟着长笛的动作舞动。
[00:59.75]We were very much surprised when the snake charmer | 当耍蛇人突然开始演奏爵士乐和现代流行歌曲时，
[01:03.83]suddenly began to play jazz and modern pop songs. | 我们感到非常惊讶。
[01:08.84]The snake, however, continued to 'dance' slowly. | 然而，那条蛇却继续缓慢地“跳舞”。
[01:14.12]It obviously could not tell the difference between Indian music and jazz! | 它显然分辨不出印度音乐和爵士乐的区别！